ng does work once the drag starts from a clear point, so I judged it a PASS. Conversely, for CT-17 the \"disabling clears the gap\" path is confounded by the stale-state bug: disabling also resets the level, so the warning clears either way. The observed outcome matched expectations, so I recorded PASS, but that specific sub-behavior isn't independently confirmed."
